<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Lithuania</h1><p class="st-meta">1251 CE – 1263 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The only crowned kingdom in Lithuanian history, created when Mindaugas accepted Catholic baptism and a royal crown from the Pope.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> had united the Lithuanian lands by the 1240s but faced a coalition of rivals backed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>. To split his enemies he accepted baptism in 1251, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iv">Pope Innocent IV</a> authorised his coronation, which took place in July 1253, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>As king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> ruled a mainly pagan land with a small Catholic church and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> appointed for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a>. He granted lands, including parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitia">Samogitia</a>, to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a> in return for its support. The kingdom brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> into the diplomatic world of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> while Mindaugas extended his power over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-ruthenia">Black Ruthenia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitians">Samogitians</a> crushed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-durbe">Durbe</a> in 1260, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindaugas">Mindaugas</a> broke with the order and seems to have abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. He was murdered in 1263 by his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treniota">Treniota</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daumantas-of-pskov">Daumantas</a>, and the royal title lapsed. The state continued as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a>; his coronation is marked by a Lithuanian national holiday.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1251 CE – 1263 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1251 CE – 1263 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mindaugas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity and Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lithuanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a href="/countries/belarus">Belarus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Mindaugas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1257&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lithuania" aria-label="Kingdom of Lithuania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5226 300 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Lithuania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5546 556L5556 562"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5556 562h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5546 556h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5546 556h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atl